# Screensaver

`screensaver` is the native clean-room terminal animation tool from
[`keys-i/tools`](https://github.com/keys-i/tools). It owns digital rain,
wrapping pipes, a frog pond, offline weather, a bounded local Git-history view,
and local GIF87a/89a decoding. It does not launch the six research programs or
copy their code, assets, themes, or branding.

Choose `snapshot` for deterministic plain or JSON output inside Scripts.
Choose `open` to show the exact command for a full terminal. Generated scenes
accept an optional `--seed`; snapshots accept `--frame`; interactive animation
can be reduced to one update per second with `--fps 1`. `NO_COLOR=1` disables
color. Keyboard controls are Space to pause, `r` to reset, arrows to navigate
or change speed, `n` to advance a mixed scene, and `q` or Escape to quit.

The `action` selects `snapshot` or `open`; `scene` selects the renderer. Supply
a `gif` file for GIF mode or an optional `repository` for Git mode, choose a
`seed` for generated scenes, and set the weather `condition` through
`--condition`. Snapshots accept
a `frame` and `format`; animation accepts `fps`. Use `--night` for the night
weather palette.

Git mode invokes only the installed `git` command once, reading at most 64
commit summaries through a 30-second, 8 MiB bounded capture. GIF input is local
and capped at 64 MiB, 512 frames, 16 million retained render pixels, and 128
million decoded source pixels. No network, geolocation, weather API, Tenor
query, video codec, media export, cache, Python, or shell process is involved.

This Scripts pack contains only the typed UI contract; all scene, parser, and
terminal behavior stays in the Rust binary. The prepared `keys-tools` PyPI
package has not been published.
